  "agents": {
    "purpose": [
      "`{{project}}` is a 3D studio workspace for Blender, Houdini, UE5, Godot and Three.js/web.",
      "Read the scoped `AGENTS.md` in `dcc/blender/`, `dcc/houdini/`, `engines/ue5/`, `engines/godot/` or `web/` before working there."
    ],
    "rules": [
      "- Run `git lfs install` before the first commit so `.gitattributes` binaries use Git LFS.",
      "- One folder per asset in the deepest existing category folder (e.g. `assets/environments/modular/<asset_id>/`), copied from `assets/_template/` with `asset.yaml` filled in.",
      "- Per asset: editable sources in `source/<tool>/`, full-res texture sources in `textures/source/`, baked textures in `textures/baked/`, turntables/thumbnails in `preview/`, and final published files in `export/` (`fbx/`, `glb/`, `usd/`, `abc/`, `vdb/`).",
      "- Never put DCC source files (`.blend`, `.hip`, `.ztl`, `.spp`) in engine or web folders; assets made in Blender or Houdini arrive there as exports from the asset's `export/` folder, while engine-native assets (Blueprints, maps, materials, `.tres`, `.gdshader`) are authored in the engine.",
      "- Supply conversion scripts before creating compressed web copies; this kit provides only destination folders.",
      "- Create `Studio.uproject`, `project.godot`, `export_presets.cfg` and `package.json` with the real tool (Unreal Editor, Godot editor, or the package manager/project scaffolder), never by hand.",
      "- Record only verified tool versions in `TOOLS.lock`.",
      "- `.agents/lanes/<agent>/` is your only scratch space for files outside the engines (unreviewed Unreal assets go in `engines/ue5/Studio/Content/_Dev/`); put handoff notes in `.agents/handoff/`."
    ]
  },
